WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.135 --> 00:00:03.903
-Republicans are once again
making a mad dash

00:00:03.903 --> 00:00:06.306
to rush through a bill
that would repeal Obamacare

00:00:06.306 --> 00:00:08.708
and drastically overhaul
health care in this country.

00:00:08.708 --> 00:00:11.210
And once again,
very few Republicans

00:00:11.210 --> 00:00:14.280
can actually defend their bill
or explain what it does.

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:16.682
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:16.682 --> 00:00:18.685 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:18.685 --> 00:00:20.853 line:0%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:20.853 --> 00:00:22.955
-There's nothing
Donald Trump is better at

00:00:22.955 --> 00:00:25.024
than making big, empty promises

00:00:25.024 --> 00:00:27.560
even though he has no idea
how to achieve them.

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:30.196
The latest example of this
strategy came yesterday

00:00:30.196 --> 00:00:32.898
when Trump met with Palestinian
President Mahmoud Abbas

00:00:32.898 --> 00:00:34.634
at the United Nations

00:00:34.634 --> 00:00:36.902
and said he'd like to achieve
Middle East peace.

00:00:36.902 --> 00:00:39.605
Although he seemed to have
no real clue how to do it,

00:00:39.605 --> 00:00:42.141
as you can tell
from his nonchalant tone.

00:00:42.141 --> 00:00:45.077
-Israel is working very hard
toward the same goal.

00:00:45.077 --> 00:00:46.312
And I must tell you,

00:00:46.312 --> 00:00:49.048
Saudi Arabia and many
of the different nations

00:00:49.048 --> 00:00:50.683
are working also hard.

00:00:50.683 --> 00:00:53.385
So, we'll see
if we can put it together.

00:00:53.385 --> 00:00:56.990
Who knows?
Stranger things have happened.

00:00:56.990 --> 00:00:59.391
[ Laughter ]

00:00:59.391 --> 00:01:01.094
-He talks
about Middle East peace

00:01:01.094 --> 00:01:03.095
the way people talk
about getting back together

00:01:03.095 --> 00:01:04.664
with their ex.

00:01:04.664 --> 00:01:07.600
Hey, stranger things
have happened, right?

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:08.668
But he's right.

00:01:08.668 --> 00:01:10.403
Not only have
stranger things happened,

00:01:10.403 --> 00:01:12.538
stranger things
are constantly happening.

00:01:12.538 --> 00:01:14.174
I think we might all be trapped

00:01:14.174 --> 00:01:16.909
in an episode
of "Stranger Things."

00:01:16.909 --> 00:01:18.544
We're a week away
from Trump saying

00:01:18.544 --> 00:01:19.912
[As Trump] we're gonna pass
health care,

00:01:19.912 --> 00:01:21.314
achieve Middle East peace,

00:01:21.314 --> 00:01:23.716
and bring Barb back
from the Upside Down.

00:01:23.716 --> 00:01:25.418
We can get it done.

00:01:25.418 --> 00:01:28.387
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:28.387 --> 00:01:30.390
[ Normal voice ] Even when
it comes to basic details,

00:01:30.390 --> 00:01:32.424
Trump is, of course,
often confused.

00:01:32.424 --> 00:01:33.793
Just take his address yesterday

00:01:33.793 --> 00:01:35.428
at a luncheon
with African leaders

00:01:35.428 --> 00:01:37.997
where he tried to praise
several African countries

00:01:37.997 --> 00:01:39.632
for their efforts
on health care,

00:01:39.632 --> 00:01:42.435
but seemed to make up a country
on the spot.

00:01:42.435 --> 00:01:44.036
-In Guinea and Nigeria,

00:01:44.036 --> 00:01:47.940
you fought a horrifying
Ebola outbreak.

00:01:47.940 --> 00:01:52.478
Nambia's health system
is increasingly self-sufficient.

00:01:52.478 --> 00:01:53.712
-Of course, the problem is

00:01:53.712 --> 00:01:56.449
Nambia is not a country
that actually exists.

00:01:56.449 --> 00:02:00.787
I'm pretty sure Trump pulled
that right out of his Djibouti.

00:02:00.787 --> 00:02:02.955
Trump is single handedly keeping

00:02:02.955 --> 00:02:05.725
Google's "did you mean" feature
in business.

00:02:05.725 --> 00:02:07.727
[ Laughter ]

00:02:07.727 --> 00:02:09.261
That's right.
Trump thinks there's a country

00:02:09.261 --> 00:02:12.698
called Nambia, which, of course,
is right next to Nigeristan

00:02:12.698 --> 00:02:14.834
and Kenya-Believe-This-
[Bleep ]-Guy.

00:02:14.834 --> 00:02:16.736
[ Laughter ]

00:02:16.736 --> 00:02:19.238
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:19.238 --> 00:02:23.876
Now, the "who knows" approach
is basically the same approach

00:02:23.876 --> 00:02:25.278
Trump has used on health care.

00:02:25.278 --> 00:02:27.580
During the campaign,
he claimed repeatedly

00:02:27.580 --> 00:02:29.348
that he would provide
great health care

00:02:29.348 --> 00:02:31.717
at a much lower cost
that would cover everybody

00:02:31.717 --> 00:02:33.519
and that it would be very easy
to pass.

00:02:33.519 --> 00:02:36.188
Well, shockingly,
it turns out Trump had no idea

00:02:36.188 --> 00:02:37.724
how to accomplish any of that.

00:02:37.724 --> 00:02:39.225
In fact, during a recent meeting

00:02:39.225 --> 00:02:41.127
where a bipartisan group
of lawmakers

00:02:41.127 --> 00:02:42.895
tried to pitch him
on a compromise bill

00:02:42.895 --> 00:02:44.364
to shore up Obamacare,

00:02:44.364 --> 00:02:46.232
all Trump cared about
was the name.

00:02:46.232 --> 00:02:47.267
According to<i> Politico...</i>

00:02:52.371 --> 00:02:54.207
A Democratic lawmaker
responded...

00:02:57.543 --> 00:02:59.412
Hell, you can call it Nambia!

00:02:59.412 --> 00:03:00.946
[ Laughter ]

00:03:00.946 --> 00:03:03.416
No one else is using it.

00:03:03.416 --> 00:03:05.051
Now...

00:03:05.051 --> 00:03:07.386
[ Applause ]

00:03:07.386 --> 00:03:09.722
Democrats and Republicans
actually were getting close

00:03:09.722 --> 00:03:11.790
to a bipartisan solution
that would have fixed

00:03:11.790 --> 00:03:13.159
some of the problems
with Obamacare

00:03:13.159 --> 00:03:14.893
while keeping the bill
largely in place.

00:03:14.893 --> 00:03:17.963
But GOP leaders decided
to blow all of that up

00:03:17.963 --> 00:03:21.434
in favor of yet again another
last-ditch effort

00:03:21.434 --> 00:03:23.703
to repeal and replace Obamacare.

00:03:23.703 --> 00:03:25.237
-A health care hail Mary --

00:03:25.237 --> 00:03:26.839
The president
pushing Republicans

00:03:26.839 --> 00:03:29.875
to not let
this Obamacare repeal fail.

00:03:29.875 --> 00:03:31.177
-This is
the Graham-Cassidy bill.

00:03:31.177 --> 00:03:32.845
This, really, for all intents
and purposes,

00:03:32.845 --> 00:03:33.980
is the final hail Mary

00:03:33.980 --> 00:03:35.882
here for Republicans
on health care.

00:03:35.882 --> 00:03:38.084
-Republicans pushing ahead
with a hail Mary plan.

00:03:38.084 --> 00:03:39.552
-This hail Mary option.

00:03:39.552 --> 00:03:41.854
-They're referring to it
as a hail Mary, essentially.

00:03:41.854 --> 00:03:45.391
-There is the last-ditch,
furious hail Mary effort.

00:03:45.391 --> 00:03:47.126
-Of course,
if this thing passes,

00:03:47.126 --> 00:03:49.595
a hail Mary might be the only
health care option

00:03:49.595 --> 00:03:51.563
some people can afford.

00:03:51.563 --> 00:03:53.065
Hail Mary, full of grace,

00:03:53.065 --> 00:03:55.868
does this mole
look weird to you?

00:03:55.868 --> 00:03:57.102
But that's right.

00:03:57.102 --> 00:03:58.638
They're throwing
another hail Mary.

00:03:58.638 --> 00:04:00.073
Except Republicans
aren't exactly

00:04:00.073 --> 00:04:01.607
Tom Brady or Aaron Rodgers.

00:04:01.607 --> 00:04:03.342
They're more like Jay Cutler.

00:04:03.342 --> 00:04:06.379
-He's gonna launch it.

00:04:06.379 --> 00:04:10.349
And that was way out of bounds.
Incomplete.

00:04:10.349 --> 00:04:11.784
[ Laughter ]

00:04:11.784 --> 00:04:13.720
-Now, the main sponsors
of this new bill

00:04:13.720 --> 00:04:15.921
are Senators Bill Cassidy
and Lindsey Graham.

00:04:15.921 --> 00:04:17.890
And they are trying
to rush it through for a vote

00:04:17.890 --> 00:04:19.058
as early as next week.

00:04:19.058 --> 00:04:20.426
Now, as you may recall,

00:04:20.426 --> 00:04:22.061
Republicans complained
repeatedly

00:04:22.061 --> 00:04:23.896
about the process Democrats used

00:04:23.896 --> 00:04:26.366
to pass Obamacare
in 2009 and 2010

00:04:26.366 --> 00:04:28.834
even though it was
a far more open process

00:04:28.834 --> 00:04:30.203
than they're using now.

00:04:30.203 --> 00:04:32.104
But they didn't just complain
about the process.

00:04:32.104 --> 00:04:35.308
They even complained about
the length of the bill itself.

00:04:35.308 --> 00:04:38.277
In fact, back in 2009,
Senator Mitch McConnell thought

00:04:38.277 --> 00:04:41.280
the page length of the Obamacare
bill was so damning

00:04:41.280 --> 00:04:42.748
that during one floor speech,

00:04:42.748 --> 00:04:44.917
he kept repeating it
over and over.

00:04:44.917 --> 00:04:47.420
-We have now had less than
48 hours

00:04:47.420 --> 00:04:52.024
to look through
this 2,074-page bill.

00:04:52.024 --> 00:04:56.295
This massive, 2,074-page bill.

00:04:56.295 --> 00:05:00.933
Buried in this 2,074-page bill.

00:05:00.933 --> 00:05:06.305
This monstrous, 2,074-page bill.

00:05:06.305 --> 00:05:09.909
On what is buried
in this 2,074-page bill.

00:05:09.909 --> 00:05:13.145
In this 2,074-page bill.

00:05:13.145 --> 00:05:17.783
Were we to pass
this 2,074-page bill.

00:05:17.783 --> 00:05:20.386
This 2,074-page bill.

00:05:20.386 --> 00:05:25.157
What else do we know
about this 2,074-page bill?

00:05:25.157 --> 00:05:27.927
-Well, there's one thing
we definitely know.

00:05:27.927 --> 00:05:29.562
[ Laughter ]

00:05:29.562 --> 00:05:31.496
But here's the thing.
It's supposed to be long.

00:05:31.496 --> 00:05:32.831
This isn't book club.

00:05:32.831 --> 00:05:35.467
You're reorganizing one-sixth
of the American economy.

00:05:35.467 --> 00:05:36.802
Details are good.

00:05:36.802 --> 00:05:38.337
Just take
Obamacare's protections

00:05:38.337 --> 00:05:40.572
for people with preexisting
conditions as an example.

00:05:40.572 --> 00:05:44.276
Obamacare had lots of very
specific legal definitions

00:05:44.276 --> 00:05:45.811
for what kinds of coverage

00:05:45.811 --> 00:05:48.147
people with preexisting
conditions should get.

00:05:55.722 --> 00:05:59.392
By comparison, the new GOP bill
has none of those details.

00:06:05.464 --> 00:06:06.565
And I don't know if you've met

00:06:06.565 --> 00:06:08.034
the guy who will be signing
this bill,

00:06:08.034 --> 00:06:11.470
but I'm not sure we should go
by his definition of affordable.

00:06:11.470 --> 00:06:13.106
[ Light laughter ]

00:06:13.106 --> 00:06:14.239
So the bill takes money away

00:06:14.239 --> 00:06:15.741
from vulnerable people
on Medicaid

00:06:15.741 --> 00:06:16.876
and strips away protections

00:06:16.876 --> 00:06:18.544
for people
with preexisting conditions.

00:06:18.544 --> 00:06:20.580
Now, you might think,
"How could any senator

00:06:20.580 --> 00:06:22.348
vote for such a monstrous bill?"

00:06:22.348 --> 00:06:25.184
Well, the answer is, they either
don't know or don't care.

00:06:25.184 --> 00:06:27.185
The website Vox interviewed
GOP senators

00:06:27.185 --> 00:06:29.222
and asked them basic questions
about the bill,

00:06:29.222 --> 00:06:30.857
and their answers were baffling.

00:06:30.857 --> 00:06:32.158
Take, for example, this exchange

00:06:32.158 --> 00:06:33.826
with Kansas Senator Pat Roberts.

00:06:46.239 --> 00:06:48.074
[ Laughter ]

00:06:54.980 --> 00:06:57.016
I love how he realized
halfway through

00:06:57.016 --> 00:06:58.450
that his analogy made no sense

00:06:58.450 --> 00:07:01.487
and he just hoped the reporter
had never seen the movie.

00:07:01.487 --> 00:07:03.555
"You see, it's kind of like
'Forrest Gump.'

00:07:03.555 --> 00:07:05.190
You probably haven't seen
that movie."

00:07:05.190 --> 00:07:06.158
"No, I've seen it."

00:07:06.158 --> 00:07:07.259
"Oh. Uh...

00:07:07.259 --> 00:07:09.128
it's like 'Minions.'"

00:07:09.128 --> 00:07:11.330
[ Laughter ]

00:07:11.330 --> 00:07:13.499
And on top of everything else
this bill would do,

00:07:13.499 --> 00:07:14.734
it would also...

00:07:22.809 --> 00:07:26.111
Now, those cuts may seem savage
and cruel, but to be fair,

00:07:26.111 --> 00:07:29.147
Republicans have always preached
fiscal responsibility

00:07:29.147 --> 00:07:30.682
and the importance
of saving money.

00:07:30.682 --> 00:07:32.985
And I'm sure
this next series of clips

00:07:32.985 --> 00:07:35.153
about Trump's Health Secretary,
Tom Price,

00:07:35.153 --> 00:07:37.556
won't prove that
they're all full of [bleep]

00:07:37.556 --> 00:07:40.325
-Health and Human Services
Secretary Tom price

00:07:40.325 --> 00:07:42.828
is taking a little bit of heat
after Politico found

00:07:42.828 --> 00:07:45.765
he took five
private flights last week

00:07:45.765 --> 00:07:49.202
for events in Maine,
New Hampshire, and Pennsylvania.

00:07:49.202 --> 00:07:52.571
The cost?
Tens of thousands of dollars.

00:07:52.571 --> 00:07:53.739
-That included a flight

00:07:53.739 --> 00:07:55.808
from Washington, D.C.,
to Philadelphia and back

00:07:55.808 --> 00:07:57.543
on a 30-seat private charter

00:07:57.543 --> 00:07:59.745
at a cost of -- and this
is really astounding --

00:07:59.745 --> 00:08:01.113
$25,000.

00:08:01.113 --> 00:08:03.182
-$25,000.

00:08:03.182 --> 00:08:06.418
Do you know how short a flight
is from D.C. to Philadelphia?

00:08:06.418 --> 00:08:07.719
If you tried to watch

00:08:07.719 --> 00:08:09.921
"Thelma &amp; Louise"
on that flight,

00:08:09.921 --> 00:08:13.025
you wouldn't meet Louise!

00:08:13.025 --> 00:08:15.761
Susan Sarandon is in it?
Not the part I saw.

00:08:15.761 --> 00:08:16.995
[ Laughter ]

00:08:16.995 --> 00:08:18.864
So, Tom Price thinks
Medicaid patients

00:08:18.864 --> 00:08:20.766
should lose their health care,
but has no problem

00:08:20.766 --> 00:08:23.168
spending tens of thousands
of dollars on private jets.

00:08:23.168 --> 00:08:24.636
And he's not the only one.

00:08:24.636 --> 00:08:28.174
Treasury Secretary Steve Mnuchin
also came under fire after he...

00:08:31.577 --> 00:08:32.678 line:0%
And before that...

00:08:37.250 --> 00:08:40.119
And when he was asked about that
taxpayer-funded eclipse trip,

00:08:40.119 --> 00:08:43.022
he tried to claim that he didn't
actually care about the eclipse

00:08:43.022 --> 00:08:45.190
because he's from New York.

00:08:45.190 --> 00:08:49.595
-When I got there, the staff
had actually intended

00:08:49.595 --> 00:08:53.833
that we watch the eclipse
on the roof of Ft. Knox.

00:08:53.833 --> 00:08:55.834
And, you know,
people in Kentucky

00:08:55.834 --> 00:08:58.103
took this stuff very seriously.

00:08:58.103 --> 00:08:59.871
Being a New Yorker
in California,

00:08:59.871 --> 00:09:01.073
I was like, the eclipse --

00:09:01.073 --> 00:09:02.941
We got there, I was like,
"Really, I don't have

00:09:02.941 --> 00:09:04.442
any interest in watching
the eclipse."

00:09:04.442 --> 00:09:07.046
-You think New Yorkers
don't care about the eclipse?

00:09:07.046 --> 00:09:08.481
I can show you one New Yorker

00:09:08.481 --> 00:09:10.115
who wanted to see the eclipse
so badly,

00:09:10.115 --> 00:09:11.717
he almost burned his retinas.

00:09:11.717 --> 00:09:14.253
[ Laughter ]

00:09:14.253 --> 00:09:16.188
[ As Trump ]
No, I don't want the glasses.

00:09:16.188 --> 00:09:19.325
I want to see the whole thing.
No glasses.

00:09:19.325 --> 00:09:21.360
[ Laughter ]

00:09:23.729 --> 00:09:25.797
[ Normal voice ] So these guys
think millions of people

00:09:25.797 --> 00:09:27.833
should have their health care
ripped away from them

00:09:27.833 --> 00:09:29.134
while they spend thousands

00:09:29.134 --> 00:09:30.803
on private jets
and eclipse trips

00:09:30.803 --> 00:09:31.970
they don't even care about.

00:09:31.970 --> 00:09:33.271
And now the question is,

00:09:33.271 --> 00:09:35.241
can they get the votes
to pass this bill?

00:09:35.241 --> 00:09:36.942
Republicans are pulling out
all the stops,

00:09:36.942 --> 00:09:39.011
even forming unlikely alliances.

00:09:39.011 --> 00:09:41.747
Lindsey Graham, for example,
said he's even been in contact

00:09:41.747 --> 00:09:43.281
with his one-time nemesis,

00:09:43.281 --> 00:09:45.484
Trump's former chief strategist,
Steve Bannon

00:09:45.484 --> 00:09:47.285
and that Bannon
has been helping him

00:09:47.285 --> 00:09:48.520
push the new repeal bill.

00:09:48.520 --> 00:09:49.655
Graham said of Bannon...

00:09:52.958 --> 00:09:55.961
Hey, Lindsay, when you're trying
to get a bill passed,

00:09:55.961 --> 00:09:57.195
you're not supposed to admit

00:09:57.195 --> 00:10:00.098
that the people
you're working with are evil.

00:10:00.098 --> 00:10:02.334
[ As Graham ] Let's just say,
Cruella de Vil and I

00:10:02.334 --> 00:10:04.170
have been working on something
that I believe

00:10:04.170 --> 00:10:06.305
will be good for all Dalmatians.

00:10:06.305 --> 00:10:07.706
[ Laughter ]

00:10:07.706 --> 00:10:09.074
[ Normal voice ] But there
is still some holdouts.

00:10:09.074 --> 00:10:12.211
Kentucky Senator Rand Paul
remains opposed to the bill

00:10:12.211 --> 00:10:14.113
because he thinks it doesn't
actually go far enough

00:10:14.113 --> 00:10:15.614
in repealing Obamacare.

00:10:15.614 --> 00:10:18.150
So, to win over votes,
Trump has been tweeting.

00:10:18.150 --> 00:10:19.185
Yesterday, he claimed...

00:10:27.292 --> 00:10:28.594
And before that, he tweeted...

00:10:36.635 --> 00:10:39.205
So, Trump managed to claim
three falsehoods in there.

00:10:39.205 --> 00:10:41.107
Bill covers
preexisting conditions.

00:10:41.107 --> 00:10:42.174
It doesn't.

00:10:42.174 --> 00:10:44.376
Graham-Cassidy Bill is great.
It's not.

00:10:44.376 --> 00:10:46.212
And Rand Paul
is a friend of mine.

00:10:46.212 --> 00:10:47.512
He is?

00:10:47.512 --> 00:10:49.348
-His visceral response

00:10:49.348 --> 00:10:51.450
to attack people
on their appearance --

00:10:51.450 --> 00:10:54.086
short, tall, fat, ugly.

00:10:54.086 --> 00:10:56.521
My goodness.
That happened in junior high.

00:10:56.521 --> 00:10:57.923
Are we not way above that?

00:10:57.923 --> 00:10:59.625
Would we not all be worried

00:10:59.625 --> 00:11:02.027
to have someone like that in
charge of the nuclear arsenal?

00:11:02.027 --> 00:11:03.428
-Mr. Trump.

00:11:03.428 --> 00:11:05.731
-I never attacked him
on his look.

00:11:05.731 --> 00:11:08.701
And believe me, there's plenty
of subject matter right there.

00:11:08.701 --> 00:11:10.335
[ Laughter ]
That I can tell you.

00:11:10.335 --> 00:11:12.471
-Plenty of subject matter
right there.

00:11:12.471 --> 00:11:14.807
Trump knows more
about Rand Paul's appearance

00:11:14.807 --> 00:11:16.842
than he knows about
his own health care bill.

00:11:16.842 --> 00:11:20.945
In fact, his Rand Paul burn book
is 2,074 pages.

00:11:20.945 --> 00:11:22.981
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:11:22.981 --> 00:11:26.151
So Republicans are racing

00:11:26.151 --> 00:11:27.586
to jam through
a health care bill

00:11:27.586 --> 00:11:29.288
that would destroy Medicaid
and strip coverage

00:11:29.288 --> 00:11:30.489
for millions of people,

00:11:30.489 --> 00:11:33.024
